PySide6 / Qt — LGPL v3 notice and relinking rights
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

PiManager uses PySide6 (Qt for Python) under the terms of the GNU Lesser
General Public License version 3 (LGPL v3). PiManager holds no commercial
Qt license; the LGPL is the license under which Qt is used here.

The Windows release is a PyInstaller *onefile* executable, and the macOS /
Linux releases are PyInstaller bundles: in all cases PySide6/Qt shared
libraries are embedded in the distributed artifact rather than resolved from
the user's system. LGPL v3 therefore requires that recipients be able to
replace or relink the LGPL-covered libraries. We satisfy that as follows.

1. Complete corresponding source for PiManager itself (the LGPL "work that
   uses the Library") is published at:
       https://github.com/suimi8/PiManager
   The exact revision of every release is tagged (vX.Y.Z).

2. PySide6/Qt is used **unmodified**, installed from PyPI at the exact
   version pinned in `requirements.txt`. Its source is available from:
       https://download.qt.io/official_releases/QtForPython/
       https://pypi.org/project/PySide6/
   (Upstream Qt sources: https://download.qt.io/official_releases/qt/)

3. To relink PiManager against a different PySide6/Qt build, install that
   build and rebuild from source — no PiManager change is needed:
       python -m pip install -r requirements.txt -r requirements-dev.txt
       python -m pip install --force-reinstall PySide6==<your version>
       python -m PyInstaller --noconfirm --clean PiManager.spec
   See BUILD.md for the full procedure. Alternatively, run PiManager
   directly from source (`python main.py`), which links against whichever
   PySide6 is installed in the environment.

4. The LGPL v3 and GPL v3 license texts accompany the PySide6 distribution
   and are also available at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html
   and https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html .

Nothing in this notice restricts the rights LGPL v3 grants you. Where this
notice and LGPL v3 conflict, LGPL v3 governs the PySide6/Qt components.

