PyInstaller — GPL with bootloader exception
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

PyInstaller is a build-time tool and is not a runtime dependency of
PiManager (it is declared in `requirements-dev.txt`, not
`requirements.txt`). The PyInstaller bootloader embedded in the frozen
executables is covered by GPL-2.0 **with the PyInstaller bootloader
exception**, which explicitly permits distributing frozen applications
under any license of the author's choosing. PiManager's Apache-2.0
licensing is therefore unaffected; no GPL obligation propagates to
PiManager's own source.
